    {
      "id": "claim_8a9ce540baae496db6d85fcb221b8ac1",
      "statement": "The application separates server-side SSR API routing from browser API routing: `apiBaseInternal` is derived from `NUXT_INTERNAL_API_BASE`, then `NUXT_API_BASE`, while the HTTP plugin selects that internal base only on the server and uses the public API base for browser requests; the public base defaults to `/api`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/plugins/http.ts#L250-L259",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a595d22a6520a9990e8f68012df0c07bdcba0bb740694ff06681850dee780014:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://nuxt.config.ts#L123-L132",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eb313c8898066535ee8f12d631656c8a04927c4586b857e410a0d15f9903735a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_80e5b853e5bb4c38910556f29cecafa4",
      "statement": "The Dockerfiles copy only the built `.output` directory into the runner stage and do not declare the internal API variables as Docker build arguments, so server-only API configuration must be supplied through the runtime process environment or deployment system rather than public build arguments.",
